From: PS5_Proton <local>
Subject: [PATCH] shell32: IFolderView::ItemCount counts the selection when asked

FolderView_ItemCount answered every item for SVGIO_SELECTION, so File Explorer's commands (PS5_Proton
pw_shell_explorer.h, Cut, Copy, Rename, Delete) and its status bar ("5 items selected") took a folder with nothing
selected for one with every item selected (console capture explorer-2026-10-16-02, Documents). The list view
counts its selected items itself; SVGIO_ALLVIEW and other flags keep today's answer.
---
diff --git a/dlls/shell32/shlview.c b/dlls/shell32/shlview.c
index e82084b..b610875 100644
--- a/dlls/shell32/shlview.c
+++ b/dlls/shell32/shlview.c
@@ -3033,10 +3033,11 @@ static HRESULT WINAPI FolderView_ItemCount(IFolderView2 *iface, UINT flags, int
 
     TRACE("(%p)->(%u %p)\n", This, flags, items);
 
-    if (flags != SVGIO_ALLVIEW)
+    if ((flags & SVGIO_TYPE_MASK) != SVGIO_ALLVIEW && (flags & SVGIO_TYPE_MASK) != SVGIO_SELECTION)
         FIXME("some flags unsupported, %x\n", flags & ~SVGIO_ALLVIEW);
 
-    *items = SendMessageW(This->hWndList, LVM_GETITEMCOUNT, 0, 0);
+    *items = SendMessageW(This->hWndList, (flags & SVGIO_TYPE_MASK) == SVGIO_SELECTION ? LVM_GETSELECTEDCOUNT
+                          : LVM_GETITEMCOUNT, 0, 0);
 
     return S_OK;
 }
